description:
metadata.rs:210-247 — filter_changes_array converts Value array entries into String (id_strs), then into Id (ids_for_fetch), looks up by id_str against a HashMap<String, &Metadata>, then maps back to Value::String for the final array. Four representations for the same underlying ID:

    Value::String      (input from the response we just built)
    -> String          (id_strs, filter-mapped from values)
    -> Id              (ids_for_fetch, for the backend call)
    -> String          (HashMap key)
    -> Value::String   (output)

The HashMap key is String not Id because the lookup is  not . So the Id allocation in ids_for_fetch is throwaway — the only place it's used is the get_objects argument.

Simpler rewrite — keep a single Id-keyed lookup:

    let ids_owned: Vec<Id> = ids.iter()
        .filter_map(|v| v.as_str().map(Id::from))
        .collect();
    let (objects, _not_found) = backend.get_objects::<Metadata>(
        caller, account_id, Some(&ids_owned), None,
    ).await.map_err(|e| server_fail_from_backend(&e))?;
    let lookup: HashMap<Id, &Metadata> = objects.iter()
        .filter_map(|m| m.id().map(|id| (id.clone(), m)))
        .collect();
    let filtered: Vec<Value> = ids_owned.into_iter()
        .filter(|id| {
            lookup.get(id).is_some_and(|meta| {
                filter_related_type.is_none_or(|rt| meta.related_type() == rt)
                && filter_metadata_type.is_none_or(|types| 
                    types.iter().any(|t| t == meta.type_name()))
            })
        })
        .map(|id| Value::String(id.as_ref().to_owned()))
        .collect();

…or just keep the existing four-representation walk if Id's hashing cost is higher than String's (it's just a newtype around String, so it isn't).

Why P4 not P3: the existing code is correct and tested. The simpler rewrite is taste — but the four-step conversion is a thinking-tax every reader pays. Worth flagging because the function is non-trivial (TOCTOU semantics, filter combinator, fall-through cases) and the data-shape complexity makes the actual logic harder to verify.

If the JMAP-ayoz.9 fix (single get_objects round-trip for created+updated union) is applied, the rewrite there is the natural place to fold this into. Mark this as opinion-adjacent — engineering basis is weak; the existing code reads fine to a Rust reader, just costs a beat.
